---
import ServicePage from "../../layouts/ServicePage.astro";
import { business } from "../../data/business.js";
---
<ServicePage
  slug="underfloor-heating"
  title="Underfloor heating"
  description={`Wet underfloor heating installed across ${business.region}, connected to your boiler and controlled room by room. Gas Safe registered engineer. Free quotes.`}
  intro="Even, comfortable warmth from the floor up, with no radiators on the walls. Ideal for kitchens, extensions, bathrooms and open-plan rooms."
>
  <h2>Why underfloor heating?</h2>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li>Warmth spread evenly across the whole room, not just near a radiator</li>
    <li>Frees up wall space for kitchen units, furniture and glazing</li>
    <li>Runs at a lower water temperature than radiators, which suits modern boilers</li>
    <li>Warm floors underfoot, perfect with tiles and stone</li>
    <li>Each room or zone controlled with its own thermostat</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>Wet underfloor heating uses pipes laid under the floor, carrying warm water from your boiler. A manifold controls the flow to each room or zone, and thermostats let you set each area to the temperature you want.</p>
  <p>It works best when it goes in during a renovation, extension or new floor, when the floor is already up. We can also add underfloor heating alongside your existing radiators, for example underfloor in the kitchen extension and radiators upstairs.</p>

  <h2>What's included</h2>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li>A visit to look at the room, the floor build-up and how it'll connect to your system</li>
    <li>Advice on the right layout and controls for the space</li>
    <li>Pipework, manifold and controls installed and connected to your heating system</li>
    <li>The system pressure tested, filled, balanced and commissioned</li>
    <li>The controls explained to you before we leave</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Working with your builder</h2>
  <p>On extensions and renovations, we're happy to work alongside your builder and floor layer so the pipework goes in at the right stage and everything is tested before the screed or floor goes down.</p>
  <p>On longer jobs you get a photo report at first fix, second fix and handover, so you have a record of the pipework before the floor goes down.</p>

</ServicePage>
